      "created_at": "2020-02-26T11:58:45Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-02-26T11:58:45Z",
      "body": "There is no real thread (except mail channels were you can have discussion threads separated within a single group). First implementation of Discuss was threaded but now all messages are linked to the same first message, considering it as a flat thread. Rationale behind that model is to avoid supporting complex discussions mechanisms where people answer to a specific message, then answer that specific answer, leading to a tree of messages. That was complex to support (model is not really difficult, more for UX and display mode).\r\n\r\nWhen you reply by email we know which message you received using the headers (in reply to / references). In livechat or discuss it is not as easy.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
